        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your patient, a 55-year-old male, admitted on 12/04/2023 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced exercise tolerance. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed partial respiratory insufficiency. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Spirometry confirmed severe airflow obstruction consistent with GOLD stage III. Treatment consisted of inhaled short-acting bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone 40mg daily), and controlled low-flow oxygen therapy. The patient responded well and was discharged in a stable condition on 13/04/2023. I recommend continuation of inhaled maintenance therapy and early pulmonology follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
